(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of economic, educational and social impact of internet shutdowns imposed across the country during the last five years;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government proposes to establish uniform guidelines to ensure that such restrictions are imposed only in exceptional circumstances?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the impact of rising inflation and indirect taxes on the purchasing power of middle-class and low-income households;
(b) if so, the details and findings thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to reduce the Excise Duty on Petrol and Diesel to provide relief to consumers; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of sanctioned, filled and vacant posts of doctors, nurses and specialists in Government hospitals, State-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of these vacancies on healthcare delivery; and
(c) the steps taken to fill these vacancies within a fixed timeline?

(a) the number of MSMEs that have ceased operations or become inactive due to GST compliance, rising input costs and other economic factors;
(b) whether Government has conducted any assessment in this regard; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of commercial coal blocks auctioned during the last five years;
(b) whether coal imports have continued despite the expansion of commercial mining;
(c) if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether any assessment has been carried out regarding the effectiveness of the commercial coal mining policy?

(a) the details of industrial investment approved under various Central schemes during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) whether West Bengal has received a proportionate share of such investments; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of internet shutdowns imposed in the country during the last three years, State-wise;
(b) the reasons for such shutdowns;
(c) the estimated economic impact of these shutdowns; and
(d) the safeguards in place to prevent unnecessary disruption of digital services?

(a) the number of National Highway projects in the State of West Bengal that are running behind schedule;
(b) the reasons for the delay; and
(c) the revised timelines fixed for completion of such projects?

(a) whether Government is aware of fertilizer shortages reported during the recent sowing seasons;
(b) the quantity of fertilizers allocated and supplied to each State, particularly West Bengal, during the last three years; and
(c) the corrective measures taken to ensure timely availability of fertilizers to farmers?

(a) the number of MSMEs that have ceased operations during the last three years;
(b) the amount of financial assistance and credit support extended to MSMEs; and
(c) the measures taken to improve access to finance and markets?

(a) whether India’s trade deficit has increased during the last three years;
(b) the measures taken to reduce dependence on imports, particularly from China; and
(c) the details of export promotion assistance provided to MSMEs, State-wise including those in West Bengal?

(a) whether the Forest Survey of India has discontinued the Anavaran – Deforestation Alert System;
(b) the extent of forest cover lost across the country during the last two years;
(c) the State-wise details of forest cover depletion (in sq. km), identifying the States with the highest losses; and
(d) remedial measures taken by Government to address deforestation?

(a) the number of villages in West Bengal, particularly in border and Sundarbans areas, that still lack reliable 4G/5G connectivity;
(b) the funds allocated and utilised for improving telecom infrastructure in the State during the last three years; and
(c) the timeline for achieving universal digital connectivity?

(a) the total number of Multi-State Cooperative Societies (MSCS) functioning in the country and the number of such societies operating in the State of West Bengal;
(b) the funds sanctioned and released to the State of West Bengal for the computerisation of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS); and
(c) whether Government proposes to introduce any new policy, in consultation with the States, to further strengthen the cooperative sector?
